      "side": 1,
      "message": "* **Location:** mpu\\_enable()  \n* **Issue:** In the Cortex-M33 block, the code only asserts the enable bit: MPU-\\\u003eRLAR |\u003d MPU\\_RLAR\\_EN\\_Msk;. Unlike the ARMv7-M block (which configures RAM locks if defined) or standard Zephyr initialization, this assumes that the MPU-\\\u003eRBAR (Base Address Register) and the rest of the MPU-\\\u003eRLAR (Limit Address and Attributes) are already perfectly configured for indices 0 to mpu\\_config.num\\_regions \\- 1\\.  \n* **Impact:** If those regions were not fully pre-configured by Zephyr initialization before this function is called, enabling them will result in unpredictable memory protection faults (MemManage exceptions).  \n* **Suggestion:** Ensure that the regions are fully configured before enabling them, or add a safety check/comment explaining where these specific regions are pre-initialized.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "b77b5c4509f6140ec7b50fe532f2997d8d3bbd59",
